<h2>Small Elliptic Curve Private Key (eMudhra incident)</h2>

<p>In October 2026, it was discovered that multiple intermediate certificates
used by the certificate authority eMudhra used private keys with very small
private key values, the smallest one being <em>d=4</em>. All affected
keys were byte-sized scalar values.</p>

<p>badkeys detects the affected eMudhra keys and similar small elliptic curve
private keys.</p>

